    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7509a623-c423-55cd-8904-ed8e23c4f2c0",
      ":question/problem": "Find the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{7}}}+3$ for $t>0$.\n\n{{selection}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Applying the sum rule, we compute the sum of the integrals of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t^{7}}}+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t &= \\int \\left(\\frac{1}{t^{\\frac{7}{2}}}+3\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\int t^{-\\frac{7}{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}t+3\\int 1\\,\\mathrm{d}t \\\\ &= \\frac{t^{-\\frac{7}{2}+1}}{(-\\frac{7}{2}+1)}+3\\frac{t^{0+1}}{(0+1)}+C \\\\ &= -\\frac{2}{5\\sqrt{t^{5}}}+3t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
